<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <AssemblyName>axcall</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Axcall</RootNamespace>
    <!-- Baseline version for local/dev builds; the release workflow
         overrides this with -p:Version from the git tag. -->
    <Version>0.2.1</Version>
    <!-- No ICU. axcall is invariant-culture throughout by design (callsigns
         are upper-cased with ToUpperInvariant, every number is parsed with
         InvariantCulture), so it loses nothing, and a self-contained publish
         then needs no libicu on the target. That is what lets the .deb declare
         a short Depends and run on a bare base image. -->
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Publish size and startup. Only when publishing for a specific runtime:
       ReadyToRun needs a RID, so a bare `dotnet publish` would fail otherwise.

       Measured on linux-x64 at 0.4.0, single-file self-contained throughout:

         plain                74.4 MB   23 ms to start
         trimmed              15.7 MB   52 ms
         trimmed + R2R        21.5 MB   21 ms      <- this
         NativeAOT             3.9 MB    4 ms

       Trimming alone is smaller but starts slower, because the runtime pack
       ships its framework assemblies ReadyToRun-compiled and trimming rewrites
       them, throwing that native code away. Putting R2R back costs 6 MB and
       buys the startup back, which matters now axcall is something you can put
       in a pipeline. NativeAOT wins on both counts but cannot cross-link
       linux-arm (armhf) from an x64 runner, and all three architectures build
       on the one runner today.

       TrimmerSingleWarn=false lists every trim warning rather than one summary.
       With TreatWarningsAsErrors from Directory.Build.props that makes any
       future reflection the trimmer cannot follow a build failure, which is the
       guard that keeps this safe. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(RuntimeIdentifier)' != ''">
    <PublishTrimmed>true</PublishTrimmed>
    <PublishReadyToRun>true</PublishReadyToRun>
    <TrimmerSingleWarn>false</TrimmerSingleWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Packet.Core" />
    <PackageReference Include="Packet.Ax25" />
    <PackageReference Include="Packet.Ax25.Transport.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Packet.Kiss" />
    <PackageReference Include="Packet.Kiss.Serial" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Axcall.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
